Title: The Canoe
Order: 9
Production Code: 1x09

INT. VANCE ESTATE - MORNING ROOM - DAY

AMB: quiet, the last house guest just departed

[[Aubrey Livingston]] reads over [[Dianthe Lusk]]'s shoulder as she opens a letter from [[Reuel Briggs]], and something in it undoes him.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(bitter)
You taunt me with his right to love and care for you.

DIANTHE LUSK
I did not do it to hurt you.

He crosses to her, and against her own better judgment, she doesn't pull away when his grief becomes physical, desperate.

Later, alone, a pale woman rises as if from the floor itself, crosses to a book on the table, writes something, and vanishes. Dianthe examines the page: a verse from Luke underlined in ink — "there is nothing covered that shall not be revealed" — signed, in a fine hand, "Mira."

EXT. CHARLES RIVER - EVENING

AMB: water lapping a canoe's hull, birdsong fading with the light

[[Aubrey Livingston]] paddles [[Molly Vance]] and Dianthe out onto the river, the water thick with lily stems.

MOLLY VANCE
(laughing, singing snatches of a tune)

Aubrey's paddle catches in the lily stems. He leans hard to free it.

SFX: a canoe overturning, a splash

MOLLY VANCE (CONT'D)
(a cry, cut short)

Molly's arms lock around him in panic. He tries to shake free of her — and over her shoulder sees Dianthe's head vanish beneath the water.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(a strangled cry)
No—

With a hard kick he breaks Molly's grip and swims for Dianthe instead, leaving her behind him in the water.

SFX: OUT
